(1)  837/    628E :                     ; What this does is swap the background nametable with the window layer in order
(1)  838/    628E :                     ; to create a third scrolling layer that appears above the foreground. However,
(1)  839/    628E :                     ; this comes at the cost of the background becoming garbled at the bottom of the
(1)  840/    628E :                     ; screen, which was likely what contributed in its removal. Internally, it was
(1)  841/    628E :                     ; known as "Plane Z", and was also the intended use of the third layout entry.
(1)  842/    628E :                     ; Presumably, this (alongside bit 3 of obRender) was what was used to achieve the
(1)  843/    628E :                     ; foreground effect seen in the Tokyo Toy Show '90. Ultimately, Sonic 2 repurposed
(1)  844/    628E :                     ; this code to draw player 2's foreground in multiplayer.
(1)  845/    628E :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1)  846/    628E :                     
