(1)  394/   12A32 :                     ; Configuration values for converting hexadecimal numbers to decimal.
(1)  395/   12A32 :                     ; The subroutines will subtract one of these values from the input value,
(1)  396/   12A32 :                     ; looping until it has caused an underflow. Meanwhile, it will keep track
(1)  397/   12A32 :                     ; of the number of iterations it took to cause that underflow, which will
(1)  398/   12A32 :                     ; represent the relevant decimal digit. The code will then repeat the entire
(1)  399/   12A32 :                     ; process with the "Hud_1..." value below it for the next decimal digit,
(1)  400/   12A32 :                     ; until all digits have been converted to decimal and written to VRAM.
(1)  401/   12A32 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1)  402/   12A32 : 0001 86A0           Hud_100000:	dc.l	100000
