(1) 1800/   49B52 :                     ; ===========================================================================
(1) 1801/   49B52 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1) 1802/   49B52 :                     ; FM Note Values: b-0 to a#8
(1) 1803/   49B52 :                     ;
(1) 1804/   49B52 :                     ; Each row is an octave, starting with B and ending with A-sharp/B-flat.
(1) 1805/   49B52 :                     ; Notably, this differs from the PSG frequency table, which starts with C and
(1) 1806/   49B52 :                     ; ends with B. This is caused by 'FMSetFreq' subtracting $80 from the note
(1) 1807/   49B52 :                     ; instead of $81, meaning that the first frequency in the table ironically
(1) 1808/   49B52 :                     ; corresponds to the 'rest' note. The only way to use this frequency in a
(1) 1809/   49B52 :                     ; real note is to transpose the channel to a lower semitone.
(1) 1810/   49B52 :                     ;
(1) 1811/   49B52 :                     ; Rather than use a complete lookup table, other SMPS drivers such as
(1) 1812/   49B52 :                     ; Sonic 3's compute the octave, and only store a single octave's worth of
(1) 1813/   49B52 :                     ; notes in the table.
(1) 1814/   49B52 :                     ;
(1) 1815/   49B52 :                     ; Invalid transposition values will cause this table to be overflowed,
(1) 1816/   49B52 :                     ; resulting in garbage data being used as frequency values. In drivers that
(1) 1817/   49B52 :                     ; compute the octave instead, invalid transposition values merely cause the
(1) 1818/   49B52 :                     ; notes to wrap-around (the note below the lowest note will be the highest
(1) 1819/   49B52 :                     ; note). It's important to keep this in mind when porting buggy songs.
(1) 1820/   49B52 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1) 1821/   49B52 :                     MakeFMFrequency function frequency,roundFloatToInteger(frequency*1024*1024*2/FM_Sample_Rate)
